@startuml
title Sequence Diagram – US 2.2.11 “Register and Manage Staff Members”

actor "Logistics Operator" as Operator
boundary "StaffController\n(API Layer)" as API
control "StaffService\n(Application Layer)" as Service
entity "StaffRepository\n(Domain/Infrastructure)" as Repo
database "PortManagementContext (EF Core)\n(Infrastructure Layer)" as DB

note over Operator
User Story 2.2.11 – Register and Manage Staff Members

"As a Logistics Operator, I want to register, update,
activate/deactivate, and search staff, so that port
personnel are correctly assigned to operations."
end note

== Register Staff ==

Operator -> API : POST /api/staff\n(StaffDTO)
activate API
API -> Service : RegisterStaffAsync(Staff)
activate Service
Service -> Repo : GetByMecanographicNumberAsync(mecNumber)
activate Repo
Repo -> DB : SELECT * FROM Staff WHERE MecanographicNumber = mecNumber
DB --> Repo : null
deactivate Repo

note over Service
Business Rules:
- Mecanographic number must be unique.
- Email must follow corporate domain rules.
- Initial status defaults to "Unavailable".
end note

Service -> Repo : AddAsync(new Staff(...))
Repo -> DB : INSERT INTO Staff (...)
DB --> Repo : Success
Repo --> Service : Staff persisted
Service --> API : 201 Created + StaffDTO
deactivate Service
API --> Operator : Staff successfully registered
deactivate API

== Update Staff ==

Operator -> API : PUT /api/staff/{mecNumber}\n(Updated StaffDTO)
API -> Service : UpdateStaffAsync(Staff)
Service -> Repo : GetByMecanographicNumberAsync(mecNumber)
Repo -> DB : SELECT * FROM Staff WHERE MecanographicNumber = mecNumber
DB --> Repo : Existing record

note over Service
If staff found → update allowed fields (email, phone, qualifications).
Otherwise → return 404 Not Found.
end note

Service -> Repo : UpdateAsync(Staff)
Repo -> DB : UPDATE Staff SET ... WHERE MecanographicNumber = mecNumber
DB --> Repo : OK
Service --> API : 204 No Content
API --> Operator : Update confirmation

== Activate / Deactivate Staff ==

Operator -> API : PATCH /api/staff/{mecNumber}/activate
API -> Service : ActivateAsync(mecNumber)
Service -> Repo : GetByMecanographicNumberAsync(mecNumber)
Repo -> DB : SELECT * FROM Staff WHERE MecanographicNumber = mecNumber
DB --> Repo : Staff found
Service -> Repo : UpdateStatusAsync(mecNumber, Available)
Repo -> DB : UPDATE Staff SET Status='Available'
Service --> API : 200 OK

note over Service
Only staff with status "Unavailable" can be reactivated.
end note

Operator -> API : PATCH /api/staff/{mecNumber}/deactivate
API -> Service : DeactivateAsync(mecNumber)
Service -> Repo : GetByMecanographicNumberAsync(mecNumber)
Repo -> DB : SELECT * FROM Staff WHERE MecanographicNumber = mecNumber
DB --> Repo : Staff found
Service -> Repo : UpdateStatusAsync(mecNumber, Unavailable)
Repo -> DB : UPDATE Staff SET Status='Unavailable'
Service --> API : 200 OK

== Search Staff ==
Operator -> API : GET /api/staff?name=John&status=Available
API -> Service : GetFilteredAsync(name, status)
Service -> Repo : QueryAsync(filters)
Repo -> DB : SELECT * FROM Staff WHERE Name LIKE '%John%' AND Status='Available'
DB --> Repo : Matching staff list
Service --> API : List<StaffDTO>
API --> Operator : 200 OK + Filtered staff list
@enduml
